{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# Seasonal Agriculture Performance Analysis\n","VOIS AICTE Batch 1 • 2026–2027\n","This notebook analyzes seasonal differences in yield, profitability, resource use, environmental conditions, crop performance and statistical relationships."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["import pandas as pd\n","import numpy as np\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","\n","df = pd.read_csv(\"../data/seasonal_agriculture_performance_dataset.csv\")\n","df.head()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 1. Dataset overview and data quality"]},{"cell_type":"code","exection_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["print(\"Shape:\", df.shape)\n","print(\"Seasons:\", dfP[\"Season\"].value_counts().to_dict())\n","print(\"Crops;\", df[\"Crop\"].nunique())\n","print(\"Missing cells:\", int(df.isna().sum().sum()))\n","print(\"Duplicate rows:\", int(df.duplicated().sum()))\n","print(df.isna().sum()[df.isna().sum()>0])"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 2. Seasonal performance comparison"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["season_summary = df.groupby(\"Season\").agg(\n","    mean_yield=(\"Yield_Tonnes_Ha\",\"mean\"),\n","    mean_profit=(\"Profit_INR\",\"mean\"),\n","    mean_rainfall=(\"Rainfall_mm\",\"mean\"),\n","    mean_temperature=(\"Avg_Temperature_C\",\"mean\"),\n","    mean_humidity=(\"Humidity_pct\",\"mean\"),\n","    mean_water_used=(\"Water_Used_m3\",\"mean\"),\n","    mean_water_efficiency=(\"Water_Efficiency_t_per_1000m3\",\"mean\")\n",").round(2)\n","season_summary"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["season_summary[[\"mean_yield\",\"mean_profit\"]].plot(kind=\"bar\", subplots=True, layout=(2,1), figsize=(7,6), legend=False)\n","plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 3. Irrigation and resource use"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["irrigation_summary = df.groupby(\"Irrigation_Method\").agg(\n","    mean_yield=(\"Yield_Tonnes_Ha\",\"mean\"),\n","    mean_profit=(\"Profit_INR\",\"mean\"),\n"    mean_water_used=(\"Water_Used_m3\",\"mean\"),\n","    mean_water_efficiency=(\"Water_Efficiency_t_per_1000m3\",\"mean\")\n",").sort_values(\"mean_profit\", ascending=False).round(2)\n","irrigation_summary"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 4. Cropá season analysis"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["crop_season = df.pivot_table(index=\"Crop\", columns=\"Season\", values=\"Yield_Tonnes_Ha\", aggfunc=\"mean\").round(2)\n","crop_season"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 5. Regional consistency"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["state_season = df.pivot_table(index=\"State\", columns=\"Season\", values=\"Yield_Tonnes_Ha\", aggfunc=\"mean\").round(2)\n","state_season"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# Count states following Kharif > Rabi > Zaid\n","consistent = ((state_season[\"Kharif\"] > state_season[\"Rabi\"]) & (state_season[\"Rabi\"] > state_season[\"Zaid\"])).sum()\n","print(\"States following Kharif > Rabi > Zaid:\", int(consistent), \"of\", len(state_season))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 6. Correlation analysis"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 7. Evidence-based recommendations\n","1. Prioritize Kharif planning where crop and location suitability support it because it has the strongest average yield and profitability in this dataset.\n","2. Evaluate drip irrigation for suitable farms because it has the highest average yield and profit, while consider cost and crop requirements.\n","3. Reduce reliance on high-water flood irrigation where practical because it has the highest average water use.\n","4. Treat Zaid as a higher-risk season because it has the lowest mean yield and negative mean profit; review crop choice, water demand and costs before planting.\n","5. Use regional and crop-level analysis rather than relying only on overall averages."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 8. Conclusion\n","The supplied data shows clear Seasonal differences in agricultural performance. Kharif performs strongest on average, Zaid weakest, and irrigation method and crop choice are associated with materially different outcomes. These are descriptive findings, not causal estimates; regression or hypothesis testing would be appropriate for stronger inference."]}],"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python"}},"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":5}